<title>CHILE: Chile February copper exports rise to $529.4 mln.</title>
<headline>Chile February copper exports rise to $529.4 mln.</headline>
<dateline>SANTIAGO 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chilean copper exports rose to $529.4 million last month from $512 million in the same month 1995, said the Central Bank in its fortnightly report.</p>
<p>Here are details of Chile's mining exports in February.</p>
<p> METAL			   Feb 1997	    Feb 1996</p>
<p> Copper			  529.4		 512.0</p>
<p> Iron			     22.5		  13.3</p>
<p> Salitre and iodine	   14.3		  12.5</p>
<p> Silver			   10.1		  11.8</p>
<p> Molybdenum		     17.2		  20.1</p>
<p> Lithium carbonate	     3.1		   2.3</p>
<p> Metallic gold and dore     27.9		  27.0</p>
<p> Gold mineral		    3.1		   5.0</p>
<p> Others			    4.6		   8.3</p>
<p> TOTAL			   632.2		 612.3</p>
<p>NOTE: All figures are in millions of dollars.</p>
<p>((-- Margaret Orgill, Santiago newsroom, 562-699-5595x212))</p>
</text>
